DISCLAIMER

This documentation describes a battery-powered electronic device built with
lithium-ion cells. Lithium-ion cells can vent, catch fire or explode if
short-circuited, over-discharged, over-charged, physically damaged, or charged
below 0 degrees Celsius. The material in this repository is provided as-is,
without warranty of any kind, and describes a personal prototype rather than a
tested or certified product. Anyone building from it does so at their own risk
and is responsible for their own safety and for compliance with any applicable
regulations.
